            "target_entity_instance": "Wadden Sea",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Most birds that breed in coastal areas build nests near the ground, and nest flooding is common (Greenberg et al. 2006b). van de Pol et al. (2010) showed that this risk has increased for six saltmarsh species in the Wadden Sea, with increases more than doubling for Eurasian oystercatchers Haematopus ostralegus, sufficient to cause population declines.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Drought events",
            "source_entity_type": "Weather_Event",
            "relation": "IMPACTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Europe",
            "target_entity_type": "Continent",
            "paragraph": "Drought has also been shown as a climate change driver affecting bird populations; for instance, drought events have been shown to favour the dispersal of the glossy ibis Plegadis falcinellus to Europe (Santoro et al. 2013) (Fig. 2).",
