            "target_entity_instance": "German Wadden Sea",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "German Wadden Sea, where coastal wetlands are very important in supporting coastal fisheries, the growth and abundance of a non-migratory eelpout Zoarces viviparus declined when summer temperatures and dissolved oxygen exceeded the upper and lower thresholds, respectively, with larger individuals the first to be harmed (P\u00f6rtner and Knust 2007).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
